abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v23.1 keeps everything in v23.0: CORE.md opens with what a
  functional world model is and follows one model of learning, read as a
  network, in eight steps, and formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean audits 96
  machine-checked results. It adds three pieces of research outside the
  core. Cooperative error identification asks whether different world models
  can expose each other's errors without a shared worldview, with a formal
  model and seeded simulations showing that a shared reference adds nothing
  when agents measure the same quantity, a great deal when they measure
  different ones, and harm when it is not commutable; a companion on acting
  under time shows why the regress of checking ends locally at the next
  decision. Models for acting in a changing world proposes what an
  intelligence keeps besides its world model (representations, objectives,
  policies, records), formalized and tested in simulations. A working space
  on the Yang–Mills mass gap, built over two days by the author with two AI
  assistants from different model families and now handed over to others,
  tests routes from the new two-dimensional O(N) decay proofs to
  four-dimensional SU(2) gauge theory and records why they close; it then
  proves, for growing graph classes and at all couplings, a monotonicity
  that a missing pinning lemma for the two-dimensional CP^{N−1} model
  reduces to, states the remaining open problems exactly, and includes a
  separate 14-result Lean package of renormalisation bookkeeping. It
  contains no mass-gap result, and no human expert has reviewed it.
  DIALOGUE.md records how the author and an AI assistant build the model
  together, now in 37 entries. The release title uses ‘simulation of
  reality’ to mean the internal model through which a system experiences and
  acts in the world, not a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal
  verification establishes implications under explicit premises; empirical,
  causal, political and normative interpretations remain open. The original
  repository material is dual-licensed under CC BY 4.0 OR Apache-2.0 as
  documented in DUAL-LICENSING.md; CC BY 4.0 is supplied here as the single
  Zenodo archival metadata value because the GitHub-Zenodo metadata path
  accepts one license value.
